# Academic Paper Search Engine

This project is a full-stack academic paper and web content search engine built with Streamlit, Elasticsearch, MinIO, and PySpark. It allows you to preprocess and index academic papers, crawl technical web sources (e.g. GeeksforGeeks, MathWorld), and generate AI-powered answers using integrated LLMs.

## Features

- **Automatic PDF Processing:** Extracts paragraphs and passages from academic PDFs.
- **Preprocessing:** Cleans and prepares paper abstracts using PySpark.
- **Indexing:** Loads preprocessed data into an Elasticsearch index.
- **MinIO Integration:** Stores PDFs and extracted passages.
- **Search UI:** Streamlit app for searching and displaying academic papers.
- **Web Crawling:** Fetches articles from websites using custom crawlers.

## Project Structure

```
.
├── Docker   
    ├── .env
    ├── docker-compose.yml
    ├── Dockerfile 
├── crawlers   
    ├── base_engine.py
    ├── crawl.py
    ├── engineering.py        
    ├── geeksforgeeks.py        
    ├── mathworld.py        
    ├── multi_crawler.py        
├── app.py           # Streamlit web app for searching papers
├── index.py         # Indexes papers into Elasticsearch
├── preprocess.py    # Preprocesses paper data with PySpark
├── papers.csv       # CSV file with academic paper data
├── process_passages.py     # CSV file with academic paper data
├── requirements.txt # Python dependencies
```

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Open Docker Desktop

Make sure **Docker Desktop** is running before continuing.


### 2. Start All Services

Open a terminal in **VS Code**, navigate to your project directory, and run:

```sh
docker compose -f Docker\docker-compose.yml up --build
```
This will start all necessary services including MinIO, Elasticsearch, and your Streamlit app. Wait until everything is fully built and running.


### 3. Upload PDFs to MinIO

Open your browser and go to the MinIO Console (usually at http://localhost:9001)

Log in using the default credentials

Create a bucket named papers if it doesn't already exist.

Upload your academic PDF files to the papers bucket.


### 4. Preprocess Data

In a PowerShell or Command Prompt window (same directory as mc.exe), run:
```sh
.\mc.exe alias set local http://localhost:9000 minioadmin minioadmin
.\mc.exe anonymous set download local/papers
```
This sets up the alias for your local MinIO instance and makes the papers bucket publicly readable so the app can access PDFs directly.

### 5. Preprocess Data

 Open second terminal
```sh
docker exec -it academic-search-app /bin/bash
```
Inside the container, run the following scripts one by one:
```sh
python preprocess.py
python process_passages.py
python index.py
```
preprocess.py: cleans raw text (e.g. abstracts).
process_passages.py: extracts and stores text passages from PDFs.
index.py: indexes metadata and file info into Elasticsearch.


### 6. Use the Search Engine

Once all scripts have completed:

    Go to the Streamlit web interface (URL shown in your terminal, usually http://localhost:8501)
    Use the search bar to explore academic papers by entering keywords in metadata and ask any related questions


## Notes

- Make sure `papers.csv` is present in the project directory.
- PySpark may require Java to be installed on your system.
- Make sure MinIO and Elasticsearch are fully running before indexing.
- Adjust Elasticsearch host/port in the code if needed.
- You can monitor logs from each container using the Docker Desktop GUI.

## Requirements

See `requirements.txt` for all Python dependencies.

